<script module>
  import Demo from "$ui/components/Demo.abide"
  import TryDemo from "$ui/demos/templating/errors/TryDemo.abide"
</script>

<main class="page">
  <h1>Error boundary — <code>&#123;#try&#125;</code></h1>
  <p class="lead">A <code>&#123;#try&#125;</code> block renders its body; if any expression throws while the body mounts, the block switches to <code>&#123;:catch&#125;</code>. The <code>&#123;:finally&#125;</code> branch always renders. Here the body re-mounts on each click (keyed by the run id), so you can throw and recover on demand.</p>
  <Demo id="try" title="<code>&#123;#try&#125;</code> / <code>&#123;:catch&#125;</code> / <code>&#123;:finally&#125;</code>" client="src/ui/demos/templating/errors/TryDemo.abide">
    <TryDemo />
  </Demo>
  <aside class="aside">
    <p>Each click bumps the run id, which is the keyed-list key, so the block re-mounts and re-evaluates from scratch. The run carries its own <code>fail</code> flag, so the body reads a fixed per-mount value rather than a shared mutable that could throw into an already-mounted block.</p>
  </aside>
</main>
